    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d758">

                <pb facs="0796" n="482" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg482"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d758-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-20T20:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 20, 1914, 8 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Department has been informed from London that British Foreign Office sees no
                    objection to German passenger steamers now lying in American ports being used by
                    the American Government, under the American flag, commanded by American
                    officers, to bring stranded Americans back from Europe. Department understands
                    that German Government is willing that this should be done. You will present
                    this matter informally to the Foreign Office and ascertain whether, in view of
                    the above facts, the French Government would be disposed to agree with the
                    British view.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d758-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d758-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, to the Ambassadors in
                    Germany and Austria-Hungary.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
